 shows Maloy up 19 points"], "rationale": "The district's R+21 lean, incumbent advantage, and Maloy's dominant fundraising and outside-spending edge all point to a comfortable Republican hold, and prediction markets price her win probability at 94-96%. A single September poll showing a 19-point Maloy lead is consistent with the fundamentals, so there is little reason to move away from a Safe R call.", "watch": "A late surge in Democratic turnout or a major scandal could narrow the margin, though the seat is very unlikely to flip.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["No expert rater lists this race; treated as safe for the party holding the seat.", "Incumbent Celeste Maloy (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Utah's 3rd District is a heavily Republican seat, with a partisan lean of about 21 points toward the GOP. Incumbent Celeste Maloy, who survived a competitive primary, faces Democrat Kent Udell along with several minor-party candidates. Maloy has raised roughly $1.45 million and benefits from about $1.3 million in outside support, while Udell has raised under $50,000 with no outside spending.\n\nA September live-caller poll of likely voters showed Maloy leading by 19 points, and prediction markets put her chances at 94 percent or higher. The candidates met in debates in early October covering monuments, nuclear energy, and affordability, but nothing in the coverage suggests a competitive race. The forecast expects Maloy to win by roughly 18 points.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0155, "margin": -18.58}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0256, "margin": -18.6}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0177, "margin": -18.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0181, "margin": -18.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0129, "margin": -18.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0141, "margin": -18.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0181, "margin": -18.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0196, "margin": -18.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0119, "margin": -